# project-memory — per-project isolated memory (agnes port of dsh evolve/memory.db)

Goal: each project's memory is physically isolated (one row has `workspace_id`).
Never leak memory across projects. One DB, N project partitions.

## Where the data lives
- DB: `$AGNES_MEM_DB` if set, else `~/.agnes/memories/projects.db`.
- CLI helper: `agnis_memory.py` (bundled in this skill dir; resolve it relative to this skill).
- If the DB cannot be opened (macOS TCC "Operation not permitted" on ~/.agnes), the agnes
  process is sandboxed: stop, tell the user to run the deploy command in a normal terminal
  (their terminal has Full Disk Access), and do NOT write cross-project data.

Resolve the helper once:
```
H=~/.agnes/skills/project-memory/agnis_memory.py   # adjust if skills live elsewhere
DB="${AGNES_MEM_DB:-$HOME/.agnes/memories/projects.db}"
```

## Determine workspace_id (the project's stable root)
1. If the user named a project, use its root path exactly as registered in the `projects`
   table (run: `python3 $H list-projects --db $DB`). Match by label first.
2. Otherwise use the current working directory / repo root as workspace_id.
3. If it's a NEW project, register it: `python3 $H register --db $DB --workspace-id <ROOT> --label <NAME>`.

## ACTION: enter (default)
On entering a project, load only THAT project's active memory — do not read other partitions:
```
python3 $H enter --db $DB --workspace-id "$WS"
```
- This prints the project's active memories (type/title/description) and bumps usage counts.
- Summarize into your working context. Cite project memory explicitly.
- If a referenced project has `quarantined`/`archived` rows, ignore them unless asked.

## ACTION: list / search
```
python3 $H list   --db $DB --workspace-id "$WS" [--status active|quarantined|archived]
python3 $H search --db $DB --workspace-id "$WS" --q "<terms>"        # FTS5, scoped to $WS only
```
The CLI always intersects FTS with `workspace_id` so results cannot cross projects.

## ACTION: save (at task end / when a lesson/decision/preference is learned)
Save into the CURRENT project partition only. Pick the right type:
- `user` = user preferences / profile facts
- `feedback` = lessons, pitfalls, "what would break"
- `reference` = stable reference (paths, ids, config, decisions)
```
python3 $H save --db $DB --workspace-id "$WS" --type feedback \
  --id <short_slug> --title "<one-line>" --body "<detail + source>" [--source-session <id>]
```
- Keep bodies concise; note the source (e.g. "Bash", "manual").
- If a fact conflicts with an existing row, update via:
  `python3 $H update --db $DB --workspace-id "$WS" --id <slug> --body "<new>"`
- To quarantine instead of delete: `python3 $H status --db $DB --workspace-id "$WS" --id <slug> --status quarantined`

## Stop conditions
- DB open failure / TCC block → stop and give the user the deploy command (below); never fake data.
- No matching project label → fall back to working-dir as workspace_id, register it, and proceed.

## One-time deploy (run in the USER's normal terminal, not the agnes sandbox)
```
mkdir -p ~/.agnes/memories
cp <workspace>/projects.db ~/.agnes/memories/projects.db     # already built + FTS + isolation-verified
# grant Terminal/iTerm Full Disk Access if the agnes process still can't open the db
```
